{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · The sweep and its two faces","loop":20.77,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[],"stops":[0.1107,0.2648,0.5325,0.8002,0.9037],"beats":[{"title":"A bar of 1","text":"A bar lies along [H](#lit:0,2). Its length is [1](#lit:6). It has two ends."},{"title":"The sweep","text":"Turn the [bar](#lit:6) to [V](#lit:1,3). That is a sweep: H to V."},{"title":"The outside face","text":"Sweep again, and follow the far end. For a bar of [1](#lit:8,9) it goes [Ω](#lit:4,10,11). That is the outside face."},{"title":"The inside face","text":"Now follow [the place](#lit:7) whose own path is [1](#lit:12,13), the bar's length. It stands [1/Ω](#lit:14,15) along the bar. That is the inside face."},{"title":"Inverses","text":"The two faces are inverses. [Ω](#lit:16) times [1/Ω](#lit:18) is [1](#lit:20,8): in a writer's letters, π/2 times 2/π. Multiplying them removes the facing. 1 has none."},{"title":"Two names","text":"Writers call the two faces central and inscribed. That is not wrong; it is DHV. The SHV concept is the sweep: no angles, no trig."}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.56,0.56,-0.56,-0.56],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":1},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":4},{"morph":5},{"morph":6},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":14},{"morph":15},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":16},{"morph":17},{"morph":18},{"morph":23},{"morph":24},{"morph":19},{"morph":25},{"morph":20}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":true,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.72,-0.06],"y":[-0.4,-0.4],"r":[0,0],"c":[null,null]}],"fill":null,"inPlace":true,"lag":0,"fx":null,"own":{"parent":-1,"parentAt":null,"follow":null,"look":-1,"lookRef":0,"phase":0,"rate":1,"spin":0,"motion":null,"onto":null,"laps":1,"start":null,"times":null,"clip":{"start":0,